{"agent_id":"pp3g-K6yV-fix-fork-bug-138-gh-138-the-kickoff-watchdog-nudge","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T06:08:45.865571519Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"52f44369-b47d-40e1-91c5-4a95fe9f7d30","comment_uuid":"020611f8-0a09-4780-a9ac-39938f347a29","author":"pp3g-K6yV-fix-fork-bug-138-gh-138-the-kickoff-watchdog-nudge","content":"Plan: Fix watchdog exit-condition bug in fork launch.rs build_watchdog_script (line 100). The current check 'if [ -f {worktree}/.kickoff-status ]; then exit 0; fi' disarms the watchdog as soon as the status file exists — and launch.rs writes LAUNCHING (line 648) BEFORE spawn_watchdog (line 670), so the watchdog always exits on its first check and the heartbeat-staleness nudge logic is dead code.\n\nApproach (option 1 from the issue): change the exit condition from file EXISTENCE to TERMINAL CONTENT. The script will read .kickoff-status and exit 0 only when its content starts with a terminal marker (DONE / FAILED / CI_FAILED / TIMEOUT — matching the existing conventions in sentinel/collect.rs classify_status and pipeline.rs probe_run_worktree). Non-terminal content (LAUNCHING / RUNNING / empty) continues to the heartbeat staleness + tmux send-keys nudge path, preserving existing behavior.\n\nScope: fork repo /home/claude-code/projects/crosslink, file crosslink/src/commands/kickoff/launch.rs + regression tests in crosslink/src/commands/kickoff/tests.rs. No hydration/hub files touched (#142 isolation). Add functional regression tests that execute the generated script: (a) terminal status DONE/FAILED/CI_FAILED => exit 0 with no nudge sent; (b) RUNNING status + stale heartbeat => nudge fires (proves script no longer exits on mere file existence). Rebuild per crosslink-fork.md (cargo install --path ... --force with lld).","created_at":"2026-08-03T06:08:45.858739676Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:rE+GrVnqh+IoVsQwJMwdA+DS7NIrHY7FhIH24QLJVsk","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgeSEJE8sI5sUYGJZymw6DFbN2